            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 3,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "Please remove trailing spaces (applies to multiple lines)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "What is a \"distributed BMC network\"?  Is there a reference/link, do we have a shared concept of this, or can you explain in this design?\nIs a \"distributed BMC network\" a collection of \"peer\" BMCs which appears to an Operator as a single BMC for operations such as power control, logs and sensor data, firmware update, user management, etc?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 8,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "We cannot be specific about the network topology here. It could range from a collection of peers, to a master with multiple satellites, or even just dual BMCs for redundancy. This design does not assume any particular topology; it only assumes that any BMC already part of the network can provision newly added BMCs."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Joseph Reynolds",
                        "email": "joseph.reynolds1@ibm.com",
                        "username": "joseph-reynolds"
                    },
                    "message": "Do I understand the design intention is for an existing \"distributed BMC network\" (which consists of at least one \"peer\" BMC) to:\n1. Validate a new BMC's integrity, and\n2. Bring the new BMC into the \"distributed BMC network\", as a new \"peer\" BMC, by provisioning it with certificates.\n\nThe design mentions new D-Bus interface.  Would this be exposed via corresponding new Redfish REST APIs?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "Your understanding of the BMC network definition in this document is correct. \n\nThe design mentions new D-Bus interface. Would this be exposed via corresponding new Redfish REST APIs?\n\nThis design does not specify the consumer of the service. It could be an internal service, such as the BMC discovery service, or an external Redfish client."
                }
            ],
