                "b7c51760000b867314376a3ac6570ac8b9f97353"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/07/83607/3",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                "username": "abhilashraju"
            },
            "createdOn": 1757915785,
            "author": {
                "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                "username": "abhilashraju"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "When I read this, the first thing that comes to mind is Factory Provisioning, where the following steps are carried out:\n\nUnique Identity Creation \u2013 generating a device-specific cryptographic identity.\n\nRoot Certificate Fusing \u2013 embedding the root certificate used for SPDM.\n\nSecure Boot Key Provisioning \u2013 programming the keys required to enable secure boot.\n\nIs this service intended to do the above functionality too?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "Everything you mentioned appears to be part of the BMC manufacturing process, which is outside the scope of our discussion. For provisioning, the prerequisite is that the target BMC already has a root certificate. The attestation process will then validate this root certificate during the SPDM handshake."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I think the concern is the overloading of the word \"provisioning\".  Are you using this word in a way that is mapped to something found in a standard, like Redfish, or is it just a word you've affixed to this behavior?\n\nI've seen provisioning used in many different contexts at different companies:\n\n- Setting up a BMC in manufacturing.\n- Enabling certain features in the BMC, such as extra capacity.\n- Integrating a BMC into a datacenter.\n- What you are describing in this document.\n\nWe should probably either reference a standard or use another verb that is less overloaded.\n\nWhat you're describing is probably a subset of \"integrating a BMC into a datacenter\".  I don't think you should use \"provisioning\" to describe a subset of what people probably think of when they typically hear the word \"provisioning\"."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 12,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "It manages the secure onboarding of BMCs into the data center infrastructure. If not 'Provisioning', 'Onboarding' seems appropriate, but alternative terminology suggestions are welcome."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "Is it PA RoT function: which perfroms the authentication and attestation of various connected devices?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 33,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "What do you mean by PA RoT? Yes, the Provisioning service will initiate the SPDM handshake to validate the BMC.\nNote: SPDM is a separate service, and Provisioningd leverages it for validation."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this certificate intended to provision certificates for all connected devices through SPDM,\nor is it limited to the BMC web/LDAP certificate,\nor does it specifically refer to the BMC\u2019s SPDM certificate, where the BMC acts as the SPDM responder?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 35,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "Once SPDM attestation is successful, we need a mechanism to establish trusted communication between BMCs. Services such as BMC aggregation require a mutually trusted, secure channel for HTTP/TCP connections. The provisioning process will handle the exchange of CA certificates to enable secure communication between BMCs in the future."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 77,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "How does the provisioing service looks like? what are the different objects and the properties of that object? Is it only provisioning state?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 77,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "Will make a PDI commit for it."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 79,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "Any OOB RF interface which is going to consume the information exposed by this service?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 79,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes there are consumers for  \"provisioned\" and \"trusted_connection\" properties exposed by this service"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ratan Gupta",
                        "email": "ratankgupta31@gmail.com",
                        "username": "ratagupt"
                    },
                    "message": "How this certificate exchange is going to happen?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "The current plan is to extend the SPDM application-specific flow to include certificate exchange."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 84,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "> extend the SPDM application-specific flow to include certificate exchange.\n\nDon't hand wave.  Write it out.  Nobody knows if you're doing anything secure or appropriate when you give vague statements like this."
                }
            ],
