                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is not written as a requirement.\n\nHow would a BMC validate itself?  If it isn't the BMC, you need to identify the actor (or actor type) here."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 38,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "This is too ambiguous of a requirement.  We already support this via sftp.  Probably not what you have in mind.\n\n\"certificate distribution\" ... does that mean the BMC is going to distribute certificates?  Probably not."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 82,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How does _this_ BMC know it can trust the SPDM results of _that_ BMC?  There is certificate exchange necessary to even set that up, isn't there?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 117,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "For any new repository, I've been saying we need at least one person outside of the primary contributing company to provide oversight.  Otherwise repositories quickly become a company-specific \"sandbox\" that nobody else can leverage."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 118,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't see bmcweb referenced, nor any reference to a standardized redfish schema (or schema set).  Please fix this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 118,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Abhilash Raju",
                        "email": "abhilash.kollam@gmail.com",
                        "username": "abhilashraju"
                    },
                    "message": "Will add the details . Plan is to use https://redfish.dmtf.org/schemas/v1/Manager.v1_23_0.yaml ModifyRedundancySet set schema. The redfish post will use /redfish/v1/Managers/{ManagerId}/Redundancy/{RedundancyId}/Actions/Manager.ModifyRedundancySet for the onboarding purpose. RedundancyId points to the unique BMC identifier."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 119,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "If the only change here is to add a new recipe, I don't think this needs to be spelled out.  If there is more to it, please elaborate."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 120,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Put this first."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 127,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I'd rather not do this at a dbus-level.  If you use the generated bindings, the whole dbus mapping is the trivial (and mostly automated) part."
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 129,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "How?  What does it mean to \"cover\" these?  How are you going to set up trusted certificate pairs in unit testing?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 131,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Are there any tests expected to be provided with openbmc-test-automation?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 133,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "I don't think \"test driving\" code is sufficient for something so security focused.  How do we know this doesn't break in 2 months?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "designs/provisioning.md",
                    "line": 134,
                    "reviewer": {
